C('period_poincare','scholze_comparison_note','not a manuscript theorem','Scholze’s pro-étale B_dR⁺ Poincaré sequence and proper smooth B_dR comparison are precise replacements using period coefficients.','B','Author-version Cor6.13 and Thm1.6 were read; base and coefficient/site changes are retained. The statement is a later comparison, not the author’s1965 formula.',['Scholze2013'],family='nonarchimedean',origin='later comparison identified by the earlier run',circulation='2012-05-15',publication='2013-05-17')
C('frob_chain','frob_derham','proof sketched','In characteristic p, Frobenius factors as O[0]→Ω•→O[0] as F_p-linear complexes; for smooth maps the correct O-linear formulation uses relative Frobenius and its twist.','B','The chain identities are direct; Cartier’s theorem gives the smooth zero-p-curvature comparison. Frobenius need not be injective for nonreduced rings.',['Katz1970'],family='connections',computation=ALG,publication='1970')
C('frob_closed','frob_derham','false as stated without the missing hypotheses','Frobenius identifies O with the kernel of d:O→Ω¹.','C','As an unrestricted assertion it fails on F_3[ε]/ε². For smooth X over perfect k the relative Frobenius version is valid; this corrected version does not identify the uncertain ink symbol.',['Katz1970'],family='connections',computation=ALG)
C('true_padic','true_padic_cohomology','open on the pages','The author expects a true p-adic cohomology theory related to rigid topology despite the failure of the immediate construction.','F','Crystalline, rigid and period-sheaf theories are several later realizations of aspects of the aspiration; the page gives no unique invariant to identify.',['Grothendieck1968','Scholze2013'],family='nonarchimedean',confidence='medium')

# First Pisa definitions and Frobenius families.
C('cartesian_crystals','crystal_project','proof sketched','Crystals are cartesian sections over nilpotent thickenings; after correction, thickenings of varying opens and Zariski stack descent are part of the construction.','A','Grothendieck1968 §4.1 states the local infinitesimal site. The preliminary global construction is superseded on c6/017.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='infinitesimal',circulation='1966 lectures',publication='1968')
C('global_pushout','global_pushout_retracted','corrected by himself later (c6/004 and017)','The initial inverse-image definition uses global pushouts of schemes, asserted to exist without further restriction.','A','The author retracts that unrestricted construction and replaces it with affine localization and stack gluing. The corrected local definition appears in the published infinitesimal-site construction.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='infinitesimal')
C('perfect_point_model','evaluation_nonfaithful','stated without proof','Finite PD crystals over a perfect field k of characteristic p are described by finite W(k)-modules/compatible finite-level systems; evaluation at k is reduction modulo p.','B','This is the standard PD-crystalline point model. Applying the same words to every ordinary absolute crystal requires the source’s lift/cofinality hypotheses; the dossier does not conflate the sites.',['BO1978'],family='infinitesimal',confidence='medium')
C('evaluation_nonfaithful','evaluation_nonfaithful','stated without proof','Evaluation of a finite W(k)-module crystal on k is not faithful: multiplication by p can be nonzero before reduction and zero afterward.','E','The explicit W(k) example verifies the claim conditional on the point model. No finite-dimensionality or freeness issue occurs in this example.',['BO1978'],family='infinitesimal')
C('charzero_etale_field','charzero_field','stated without proof','An algebraic extension k/Q is formally étale and has unique nilpotent lift behavior, unlike a general characteristic-zero field with transcendence.','E','The inserted algebraicity restriction belongs to this case. A transcendental field can have nonzero Ω_(k/Q), so the unrestricted field statement would not follow.',['EGAIV4'],family='infinitesimal')
C('etale_final','etale_completion_examples','proof sketched','For an étale map the infinitesimal lifting problem has a unique solution, giving the proposed final object in the relative thickening category.','E','Formal étaleness gives the exact lifting property; no claim of global closed embedding for an arbitrary unramified map is needed.',['EGAIV4'],family='infinitesimal')
C('formal_completion','etale_completion_examples','proof sketched','For a closed immersion in a noetherian ambient scheme, compatible finite infinitesimal neighborhoods describe coherent formal data; the unramified case reduces locally to this situation.','A','The noetherian formal coherent category is the relevant completion formalism. The literal reversal of S in R is retained as a reading question.',['EGAIII1','StacksExistence'],family='infinitesimal',publication='1961')
C('stratification_cocycle','stratification_definition','proved there','A stratification is a compatible system on infinitesimal diagonals satisfying the triple-diagonal cocycle; a pseudo-stratification without the cocycle is weaker.','E','The definition and its distinction are checked against the smooth comparison formalism.',['BO1978'],family='connections')
C('unramified_stratification','stratification_definition','proof sketched','For a formally unramified morphism, its infinitesimal diagonal neighborhoods are the diagonal, so the ordinary stratification is unique.','E','The assertion follows from vanishing infinitesimal diagonal ideal in this setting; it does not make absolute crystal evaluation faithful.',['EGAIV4','BO1978'],family='connections')
C('smooth_crystal_stratification','smooth_crystal_strat','stated without proof','Smooth ordinary infinitesimal crystals are described by ordinary stratifications; for the PD site, the corresponding structures are HPD stratifications/quasi-nilpotent integrable connections.','B','BO4.12 and6.6 establish the precise PD statements; Grothendieck1968 supplies the ordinary framework. Their categories and base hypotheses differ.',['BO1978','Grothendieck1968'],family='connections')
C('singular_fibred_extension','smooth_crystal_strat','open on the pages','Extend the smooth comparison to flat locally finitely presented maps, remove smoothness in characteristic zero, or replace modules by an arbitrary fibred category.','C','The standard smooth theorems do not settle these blanket extensions. For a general fibred category descent must first be added; singular modules require a separate theorem. No exact universal result matched.',['BO1978','Grothendieck1968'],family='connections',confidence='medium')
C('cartier_descent','cartier_frobenius','stated without proof','For a smooth characteristic-p morphism, modules on the Frobenius twist are equivalent to quasi-coherent modules with integrable connection of zero p-curvature.','B','Katz1970 Thm5.1 is the precise Cartier descent result. It classifies one Frobenius descent, not all ordinary stratifications.',['Katz1970'],family='connections',publication='1970')
C('iterated_frobenius','cartier_frobenius','proof sketched','Over a smooth variety over an algebraically closed field of characteristic p, locally free stratified sheaves correspond to compatible infinite Frobenius-divided locally free sheaves.','B','Gieseker1975 Thm1.3 (attributed to Katz) supplies the precise repeated-descent theorem. The infinite compatibility is essential.',['Gieseker1975'],family='connections',circulation='received 1973-02-19',publication='1975')
C('integral_connection_counterexample','charzero_counterexample_idea','not a manuscript assertion','On Z[x], the rank-one integrable connection ∇e=e dx admits no integral ordinary stratification inducing it: the order-two Taylor coefficient would be1/2.','C','The earlier-run example is independently reproved. It refutes replacement of Q-base by arbitrary characteristic-zero rings, not the smooth Q-equivalence.',['BO1978'],family='connections',origin='idea of the earlier run, rechecked here')
C('absolute_basechange','absolute_base_change','proof sketched','For characteristic-p schemes, nilpotent thickenings have p nilpotent, so their absolute coefficient map factors through an appropriate Z/p^n and hence Z_p; a W(k)-structure needs perfect-field lifting data.','A','The local crystalline framework validates the stated coefficient reductions under these hypotheses. Arbitrary additional field structures are not automatic.',['Grothendieck1968','BO1978'],family='infinitesimal')

# Restricted PD site and its local calculation (kept distinct from ordinary Inf).
C('retractive_site','restricted_sites','stated without proof','The restricted PD site consists of nilpotent truncated PD thickenings which admit local retractions; the retraction is not chosen as part of the object. Formal smoothness is invoked to compare it with the unrestricted site.','C','Local lifting explains the proposed comparison in the smooth setting. The manuscript’s exact truncated category and its ambient base must be fixed before an equivalence is assigned; modern PD and ordinary Inf results are not interchangeable.',['BO1978','Grothendieck1968'],family='sites',confidence='medium')
C('site_finite_limits','site_limits_question','open on the pages','The displayed DR categories are asserted to have fiber products/equalizers; existence in the Cris/Strat variants is doubted.','F','The differently abbreviated object categories are not all defined securely enough to classify this doubt as a theorem or counterexample. PD-envelope existence gives constructions in modern specified categories, not an automatic answer to every label.',['StacksPDEnvelope'],family='sites',confidence='low')
C('cech_cover','cech_nerve','proof sketched','The locally retractive thickening object covers the terminal sheaf, and its powers are ind-represented by the two-index system of diagonal PD envelopes and truncations, yielding the stated Čech spectral sequence.','C','The covering/nerve method survives in the published site machinery. Exact indexing and transition maps on the draft need care; ind-representability is not representability by one finite thickening.',['BO1978','Liu2025'],family='sites',confidence='medium')
C('localized_site_cohom','local_cohomology','open on the pages (à vérifier)','The localization of the restricted crystalline topos at (U,U′) is expected to have structure-sheaf cohomology equal to Zariski cohomology on U′.','B','BO5.27 and the localization argument in7.1 establish the modern PD calculation under its site hypotheses. The draft’s retractive/truncated variant is compared conditionally, not identified by notation alone.',['BO1978'],family='sites',confidence='medium')
C('affine_inverse_limit','local_cohomology','proof sketched','Affine diagonal thickenings and a countable cofinal inverse system of surjective coordinate maps give vanishing higher inverse-limit terms and compute the cosimplicial function complex.','C','The countable surjectivity argument justifies this step when its hypotheses hold. The source’s two-index transition system is not proved to satisfy them in every variant; arbitrary inverse limits are not exact.',['BO1978','BhattScholze2015'],family='sites',confidence='medium')
C('site_hypercohomology','local_cohomology','proof sketched','The local cosimplicial structure algebras globalize to Zariski hypercohomology calculating the indicated site cohomology.','B','BO7.1 gives the precise PD de Rham comparison after smooth embedding. Liu2025 §4/§11 gives an ordinary completed-infinitesimal comparison in characteristic zero; it is a separate contemporary source.',['BO1978','Liu2025'],family='sites',confidence='medium')
C('site_points','points','open on the pages','Determine the points of the various topoi in the initial comparison diagram.','C','Liu2025 Remark2.2 describes a conservative family of stalk evaluations on the ordinary infinitesimal site. That is not a classification of every point of all the diagram’s topoi.',['Liu2025'],family='sites',circulation='2025-12-02',confidence='medium')

# Dieudonné structures, lattices and generic fibers.
C('f_crystal_family','dieudonne_families','open on the pages','An F-crystal is a crystal with F:M^(p)→M; adding V with FV=VF=p is proposed to describe p-divisible groups and algebraic families of Dieudonné modules.','B','Dieudonné-crystal classification is established with finite locally free PD objects and exact base hypotheses. DeJong1995 MainTheorem1 treats formally smooth adic characteristic-p bases of the specified finite type; the1998 erratum repairs a proof lemma. This does not classify arbitrary F-crystals.',['deJong1995','deJongErratum1998','Messing1972'],family='dieudonne',publication='1972;1995;1998')
C('fv_literal','fv_readings','false as stated for the intended nonzero p-local category','The early displayed relations read FV=p and VF=1.','C','Associativity gives pF=F, so F=0 because p−1 is a unit; then VF=1 forces the object to be zero. This argument also respects semilinear twists because Frobenius fixes p. Later pages use the symmetric relation. This is a reading alarm, not a unilateral correction of ink.',family='dieudonne')
C('rational_bicrystal','isogeny_rationalization','proof sketched','For fixed weight i and finite-dimensional K=W(k)[1/p]-spaces, a symmetric FV=VF=p^i bicrystal is determined by invertible semilinear F, with V=p^iF^−1. Forgetting V is fully faithful.','E','The algebraic identity and morphism condition prove the assertion. The perfect-field point and finite rank are retained.',['deJong1995'],family='dieudonne')
C('isogeny_quotient','isogeny_rationalization','proof sketched','In the finite W-module setting, tensoring Hom with Q identifies the isogeny category with the appropriate quotient by p-power torsion.','E','Finite generation bounds the torsion exponent and allows denominator clearing. The unrestricted direct-sum example shows why an arbitrary torsion subcategory cannot be substituted.',['deJong1995'],family='dieudonne')
C('unbounded_torsion','unbounded_torsion_idea','not a manuscript assertion','For M=⊕_(n≥1)W/p^n, id_M is killed by no power of p, so remains nonzero in End_W(M)⊗Q even though M is a torsion module.','C','This independently rechecked counterexample refutes only the unrestricted quotient extrapolation; it is not asserted to be an object of every complete crystal category.',family='dieudonne',origin='idea of the earlier run, rechecked here')
C('rational_dual','isogeny_rationalization','proof sketched','For an invertible σ-semilinear F, the rational dual has F∨(λ)(m)=σ(λ(F^−1m)); the corresponding V is determined by the weight.','E','Semilinearity and preservation of the evaluation pairing are checked directly. Integral Cartier duality and arbitrary finite-module W-duality are different functors.',['deJong1995'],family='dieudonne')
C('integral_dual_failure','integral_dual_idea','not a manuscript assertion','For M=W/p, Hom_W(M,W)=0, but the dual of M/pM over k is k.','E','The exact elementary calculation shows that naive dualization need not commute with evaluation for finite modules; finite locally free hypotheses repair it.',family='dieudonne',origin='idea of the earlier run, rechecked here')
C('h1_dieudonne','h1_dieudonne','open on the pages','The H¹ invariant of an abelian variety should recover its p-divisible-group Dieudonné module.','B','Oda1969 Cor5.11 identifies H¹_dR over a perfect field with the Dieudonné module of p-torsion and its filtration. Messing’s later PD crystalline construction supplies the integral framework; the two results are not collapsed into one mod-p statement.',['Oda1969','Messing1972'],family='dieudonne',publication='1969;1972')
C('bounded_f_lattice','effective_lattices','proof sketched','For a finite-dimensional isocrystal over a complete DVR with valuation-preserving σ, all positive F-orbits are bounded iff some W-lattice is F-stable.','E','The finite-basis sum ΣF^nL_0 is bounded, finite over W and spans M; the converse is immediate. The full proof is supplied, independent of a finite numerical test.',family='dieudonne')
C('bounded_fv_lattice','effective_lattices','proof sketched','For fixed i≥0 and V=p^iF^−1, bounded F- and V-orbits yield a common stable lattice; after allowing i sufficiently large an F-stable lattice becomes an effective bicrystal lattice.','E','F and V commute with product p^i, so mixed words reduce to scalar multiples of pure words. The finite-basis bounded-lattice proof and denominator clearing are supplied. It is a pointwise statement.',family='dieudonne')
C('tate_effectivity','effective_lattices','stated without proof','Every finite-dimensional invertible semilinear F becomes effective after multiplying F by a sufficiently large power of p and choosing a suitable weight.','E','Choose any lattice, clear denominators of F to make p^aF preserve it, then clear those of its inverse by the weight. This does not produce one uniform exponent for an unspecified family.',family='dieudonne')
C('nilinvariance_lift','nilinvariance_lifts','proof sketched','The ordinary infinitesimal crystal category is asserted invariant under nilpotent thickenings, and crystals on a smooth affine lift are described by compatible higher stratifications.','A','Grothendieck1968 discusses ordinary Inf invariance and later PD modification. BO’s PD smooth-envelope comparison is a separate precise theorem; it does not justify an arbitrary ordinary/PD identification.',['Grothendieck1968','BO1978'],family='infinitesimal',confidence='medium')
C('proper_algebraization','proper_algebraization','proof sketched','Given an actual proper scheme over a complete noetherian base, coherent formal modules with compatible finite-order stratification maps algebraize, including cocycle identities.','A','Grothendieck existence algebraizes the module and each map on the proper finite diagonal neighborhoods; full faithfulness reflects the identities. The argument assumes the proper lift already exists.',['EGAIII1','StacksExistence'],family='essential_image',publication='1961')
C('stratified_free_smooth','stratified_local_freeness','stated without proof','On any finite-type k-scheme, a coherent module with a full ordinary stratification is locally free, without a smoothness hypothesis.','B','BO1978 Proposition2.16 and Note2.17 give the exact result. The Artin-neighborhood descent argument was read and rechecked; faithfully flat field extension reduces to rational closed points. Gieseker begins with locally free modules and is not the proof of this stronger assertion.',['BO1978'],family='essential_image',confidence='high',publication='1978')
C('singular_freeness','stratified_local_freeness','open on the pages','Do the asserted local freeness and noetherian-category properties survive without smoothness or with broader crystal categories?','C','The ordinary finite-type-field local-freeness part is settled by BO2.17 even for singular X. It does not extend to arbitrary PD crystals; Esnault–Shiho exhibit a nonfree lattice of a trivial isocrystal. The remaining broad noetherian assertion still requires an exact category.',['BO1978','EsnaultShihoLattices','EsnaultShiho2018'],family='essential_image',confidence='high')
C('connection_not_free','local_freeness_test_idea','not a manuscript assertion','The coherent k[x]-module k[x]/(x^p), with connection induced by d, has zero p-curvature and is not locally free.','C','The ideal(x^p) is stable under d, so the connection descends; ∂^p acts as zero. This tests a connection-category extrapolation only, since a full ordinary stratification has not been supplied.',family='essential_image',origin='idea of the earlier run, rechecked here')
C('proper_monodromy','proper_monodromy','proof sketched','With a proper smooth lift and an embedding of the characteristic-zero fraction field into C, trivial monodromy should imply constancy of the corresponding connection, followed by descent.','C','The complex proper connection argument is valid within Riemann–Hilbert; its descent and membership in the integral/ordinary crystal image remain additional steps. Esnault–Shiho results give specified positive-characteristic constancy theorems, not the unrestricted implication on the page.',['EsnaultShiho2018'],family='essential_image',confidence='medium')
C('generic_faithfulness','generic_essential_image','stated without proof','The finite isocrystal functor into stratified modules or connections on a generic fiber is asserted fully faithful; an actual proper lift and a formal/rigid lift are treated separately.','C','A fixed integral stratified lattice gives injectivity and bounded-denominator comparisons, and proper algebraization is available. The exact blanket full-faithfulness statement across all draft categories was not matched. Modern convergent/Inf/PD categories must not be conflated.',['BO1978','EsnaultShiho2018','StacksExistence'],family='essential_image',confidence='medium')
C('generic_essential_image','generic_essential_image','open on the pages','Characterize which generic-fiber connections or higher stratifications arise from integral crystals; unrestricted essential surjectivity is called too optimistic.','C','Quasi-nilpotence, convergence and Frobenius-divisibility impose different precise conditions in later theories. No one of them is silently declared the essential image of every version on these pages.',['BO1978','EsnaultShiho2018','Berthelot2010'],family='essential_image',confidence='medium')
C('frobenius_lifts','frobenius_lift','proof sketched','A smooth affine formal lift admits lifts of relative Frobenius; two choices induce canonically isomorphic pullback functors on stratified objects.','B','Infinitesimal smooth lifting gives existence level by level, and the stratification supplies the comparison between choices. BO’s stratification formalism checks the required cocycle.',['BO1978'],family='connections')
C('all_prime','all_prime_structure','open on the pages','Attach to a single crystal weight-i F_p,V_p data over every special fiber at a prime p.','F','This defines a suggested arithmetic structure, but no cross-prime compatibility, realization category or classification theorem is stated. It is not identified with a later theory of motives.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='dieudonne',confidence='low')
C('qc_site_crystals','local_site_definition','proof sketched','Quasi-coherent modules on the corrected ringed infinitesimal site correspond to cartesian quasi-coherent systems; arbitrary sheaves have noninvertible transition maps.','A','The distinction appears in the published infinitesimal-site framework. Liu2025 Remark6.2 explicitly states the quasi-coherent/crystal characterization, citing Berthelot1974.',['Grothendieck1968','Liu2025'],family='infinitesimal')
C('ordinary_cohomology','ordinary_cohomology_retracted','corrected by himself later (margin c6/018)','Ordinary crystallogenic cohomology of O is hoped to recover de Rham in all characteristics, with properness in characteristic p.','A','The author’s margin says it works in characteristic zero but not characteristic p without divided powers. Grothendieck1968 §6.5–7.2 gives the published failure and replacement.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='sites',circulation='1966 lectures',publication='1968')
C('gauss_manin_integrability','gauss_manin','open on the pages','For a smooth morphism, the canonical Gauss–Manin connection on relative de Rham cohomology should be integrable algebraically.','B','Katz–Oda1968 Thm1 proves the connection and integrability for smooth X/S with smooth S over a field. The statement is not extended here to every singular base.',['KatzOda1968'],family='gauss_manin',circulation='communicated 1968-04-19',publication='1968')
C('derham_leray','gauss_manin','open on the pages','Construct the entire Leray spectral sequence algebraically in de Rham cohomology with Gauss–Manin coefficients.','B','Katz–Oda1968 Thm3 and the addendum attributed to Deligne supply the algebraic spectral sequence; the addendum removes the affine restriction in their construction.',['KatzOda1968'],family='gauss_manin',publication='1968')
C('derived_crys','derived_crystalline_program','open on the pages','For proper smooth f, seek a perfect crystalline derived object with de Rham comparison, functoriality, Künneth and arbitrary derived base change.','B','Modern PD crystalline theory establishes the precise successor under the specified PD-base, smooth/quasicompact and flat-coefficient hypotheses. BO7.1,7.8,7.11 are the checked comparison/base-change statements. This is a replacement of the ordinary site.',['BO1978'],family='gauss_manin',publication='1978',confidence='medium')
C('individual_basechange','frobenius_duality_weights','stated without proof','Individual cohomology modules are expected to commute with all rational base change.','C','Derived base change alone does not imply this: one needs flatness or degeneration hypotheses eliminating Tor terms. BO7.13 makes the spectral-sequence issue explicit; no universal individual-base-change assertion is certified.',['BO1978'],family='gauss_manin',confidence='medium')
C('frobenius_duality_weight','frobenius_duality_weights','corrected by himself later','A duality-defined V is asserted to satisfy FV=VF=p^(2d), and each H^i is tentatively assigned an integral weight-i bicrystal.','C','The author withdraws automatic integral weight-i structures and invokes polarization/Lefschetz only up to isogeny. The p^(2d) normalization must be read with his Tate convention; no modern normalization is silently substituted.',['BO1978','Grothendieck1968'],family='gauss_manin',confidence='medium')
C('nonproper_cohomology','monsky_program','open on the pages','Denominators in Monsky–Washnitzer invariance suggest a rational nonproper theory and perhaps an enlarged crystal category.','C','Later overconvergent/rigid theories provide precise frameworks, but the draft has no definition sufficiently specific to identify a single theorem. The Numdam search found historical treatments, not a literal equivalence.',['Illusie1976','VanDerPut1986'],family='nonarchimedean',confidence='medium')

# Abelian and p-divisible deformation proposals, including their retractions.
C('h1_lift_independence','h1_lift_independence','corrected by himself later (c6/023–024 versus027–030)','H¹_dR of an abelian lift is claimed canonically independent of the lift across every nilpotent thickening, with rank2g and gluing after removing affineness.','A','This unrestricted ordinary-crystal proposal is retracted by the modular argument. The PD-conditioned invariant is the later crystalline replacement, not a restoration of the original quantifier.',['Grothendieck1968','Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation')
C('hodge_lift_deformation','hodge_deformation','open on the pages','Lifts of an abelian or p-divisible object should correspond to lifts of its Hodge filtration, while the filtration itself is not crystalline.','B','MessingV1.1–1.6 proves the p-divisible equivalence for locally nilpotent PD thickenings with p locally nilpotent and admissible locally free quotient filtration. Serre–Tate gives the abelian bridge. Arbitrary ordinary thickenings are excluded.',['Messing1972','KatzSerreTate1981'],family='abelian_deformation',publication='1972;1981')
C('serre_tate','serre_tate_deformation','stated without proof','If p is nilpotent on R and I⊂R is nilpotent, abelian schemes over R are equivalent to an abelian scheme over R/I plus a lift of its p-divisible group and the identification on R/I.','B','Exact theorem: Katz1981 Thm1.2.1 (Serre–Tate), also MessingV2.3. No Hodge-filtration assertion is built into this equivalence alone.',['KatzSerreTate1981','Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',publication='1972;1981')
C('universal_abelian_extension','universal_extension_abelian','proof sketched','An abelian scheme has a universal vector extension, functorial and compatible with base change; its Lie algebra is dual to the Hodge extension.','B','MessingIV1.23 andIV2.8 give the abelian construction and crystalline framework. This is separated from the false universal ordinary group-crystal assertion.',['Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',publication='1972')
C('group_crystal_ordinary','universal_extension_abelian','corrected by himself later','The entire universal extension group is asserted lift-independent over all ordinary thickenings, with a lifted vector subspace recoverable as a vector subgroup.','C','The later retractions prohibit treating this as proved. In characteristic p, tangent subspaces do not in general determine vector subgroup schemes. The PD Lie-crystal theorem has different content.',['Messing1972','Grothendieck1968'],family='abelian_deformation')
C('group_infinitesimal_rigidity','group_rigidity_revisions','corrected by himself later (marked faux)','The universal extension G(A) is claimed to have no infinitesimal automorphisms over arbitrary bases.','F','The page itself marks the assertion false. It does not supply a securely isolated counterexample or retain a corrected general theorem; none is manufactured in this consolidation.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='medium')
C('first_order_independence','group_rigidity_revisions','open on the pages (à vérifier, peut-être faux)','The proposed lift-independence/deformation assertions are said to hold to first order, at least over split square-zero extensions D(J).','C','The manuscript explicitly withdraws confidence. Modern PD deformation statements settle a specified square-zero PD case, not every group-level assertion in this sentence.',['Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='medium')
C('modular_obstruction','modular_counterargument','proof sketched','There is no universal ordinary stratification on H¹_dR of all elliptic families, functorial in the family and compatible with base change and Frobenius endomorphisms.','A','Grothendieck1968 §3.5 p.330 gives the same modular-family F² obstruction. The smooth integral modular-base formulation is the checked published result; the revised dimension-zero scribble is not separately certified.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='abelian_deformation',circulation='1966 lectures',publication='1968')
C('ordinary_lift_independence','ordinary_retreat','corrected by himself later (canceled conjecture)','The initial ordinary abelian case is proposed to have lift-independent G(B) over every Artinian thickening.','C','The block is canceled with a negative margin. Selecting a canonical Serre–Tate lift is a different assertion from independence of all lifts, and does not rescue the canceled conjecture.',['KatzSerreTate1981'],family='abelian_deformation')
C('ordinary_equal_characteristic','ordinary_retreat','open on the pages','Perhaps an everywhere-ordinary family in characteristic p admits the desired canonical ordinary stratification, even though it cannot extend across supersingular points or arbitrary mixed-characteristic thickenings.','C','The author retains this narrower possibility but identifies Frobenius and gluing gaps. Serre–Tate ordinary deformation parameters do not prove this full natural-stratification assertion.',['KatzSerreTate1981','Grothendieck1968'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='medium')
C('purity_gluing','ordinary_retreat','corrected by himself later (canceled or qualified argument)','A stratification on the ordinary locus is expected to extend by purity/arithmetic gluing across the missing supersingular points.','F','The argument is canceled and later explicitly qualified by uncertainty about Frobenius compatibility. No independent purity theorem with these exact data was matched.',['Grothendieck1968'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='low')
C('universal_bt_extension','bt_universal_extension','open on the pages','A p-divisible group should admit a universal vector extension, functorial and compatible with base change, with a Lie Hodge sequence controlled by the dual group.','B','MessingIV1.10,1.13–1.15 prove the construction for p locally nilpotent on the base, and identify the vector term by invariant differentials of the Cartier dual. The draft’s unspecified additive formal coefficient object is not automatically identical.',['Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',publication='1972')
C('bt_hom_additive','bt_universal_extension','stated without proof','If p is locally nilpotent on the base, Hom(G,M)=0 for a p-divisible group G and a quasi-coherent additive vector group M.','B','MessingIV1.7 proves this: locally p^N kills M while multiplication by p^N on G is an epimorphism. The page’s broader residual-characteristic wording requires this qualification.',['Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',publication='1972')
C('bt_h2','bt_universal_extension','open on the pages','The relevant group-complex H² with additive formal coefficients is expected to be locally free and controlled by the dual tangent module.','F','The additive formal object and comparison between the displayed H² and the extension functor are explicitly undefined. Messing’s Ext construction provides a precise replacement, not an exact identification of an undefined complex.',['Messing1972'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='low')
C('adic_effectiveness','adic_bt_deformation','stated without proof','The universal-extension Lie invariant passes to separated complete noetherian adic bases by inverse limit.','B','Messing’s finite-level construction and effective inverse systems of p-divisible groups supply the standard adic framework; all compatibility and finite locally free conditions remain essential.',['Messing1972','deJong1995'],family='abelian_deformation',confidence='medium')
